.TH CUPS-LPD 8 "2026-11-18" "Presswork 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
cups\-lpd \- Presswork RFC 1179 LPD-to-IPP compatibility daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/cups/daemon/cups\-lpd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cups\-lpd
is a hardened mini-server that accepts legacy Line Printer Daemon (RFC 1179)
requests on standard input/output \(en typically launched per connection via
.BR systemd.socket (5)
.RI ( cups\-lpd.socket
and
.IR cups\-lpd@.service )
or
.BR inetd (8)
\(en and forwards them to the local Presswork
.BR cupsd (8)
scheduler over IPP on
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.PP
Unlike legacy in-RAM implementations, Presswork's
.B cups\-lpd
streams incoming print jobs directly to a bounded temporary spool file created
with mode
.B 0600
and
.B O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW
(automatically deleted on exit), sanitizes control-file fields, validates queue
names against URI/header injection, and queries real queue state and job
cancellation over IPP.
.SH SUPPORTED RFC 1179 COMMANDS
.TP
.BR 0x01 " (Print waiting jobs)"
Validates the queue name and returns an RFC 1179 acknowledgment byte.
.TP
.BR 0x02 " (Receive a printer job)"
Supports both control-before-data
.RB ( 0x02 " then " 0x03 )
and data-before-control
.RB ( 0x03 " then " 0x02 )
subcommand orders, plus subcommand
.B 0x01
(abort job).
Parses RFC 1179 control-file lines
.RB ( H
originating host,
.B P
user,
.B J
job title,
.B N
filename, and format commands
.B l
raw,
.B o
PostScript,
.BR f / p
plain text, plus copy count) and submits an IPP
.B Print\-Job
request to
.IR /printers/<queue> .
.TP
.BR 0x03 " / " 0x04 " (Send queue state: short / long)"
Queries
.BR cupsd (8)
via IPP
.B Get\-Jobs
.RB ( which\-jobs=not\-completed )
and formats live BSD-compatible queue listings, honoring optional user and
job-ID filters.
.TP
.BR 0x05 " (Remove jobs)"
Translates job IDs, usernames, or
.B \-all
requests into IPP
.B Cancel\-Job
operations against
.IR /printers/<queue> .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IPP_PORT
Local TCP port on
.B 127.0.0.1
where
.BR cupsd (8)
listens (default:
.BR 631 ).
Must be a strictly numeric integer in
.BR 1..65535 ;
non-numeric or injection values cause immediate exit with failure.
.TP
.B CUPS_LPD_MAX_SIZE
Maximum accepted LPD job payload size in bytes (default:
.B 104857600
/ 100 MiB).
Jobs exceeding this limit are rejected cleanly without exhausting memory.
.TP
.B CUPS_LPD_TIMEOUT
Socket I/O timeout in seconds when communicating with
.BR cupsd (8)
(default:
.BR 60 ).
.SH SYSTEMD ACTIVATION
Enable the loopback LPD listener only if legacy RFC 1179 clients require it:
.PP
.EX
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now cups\-lpd.socket
.EE
.PP
By default,
.I cups\-lpd.socket
binds
.B 127.0.0.1:515
and
.B [::1]:515
with
.B Accept=yes ,
.B MaxConnections=64 ,
and
.B MaxConnectionsPerSource=16 .
Each connection runs under
.I cups\-lpd@.service
as unprivileged
.B User=lp
/
.B Group=lp
with empty
.B CapabilityBoundingSet= ,
.B ProtectSystem=strict ,
.B PrivateDevices=true ,
.B UMask=0077 ,
.B MemoryMax=64M ,
and
.B TasksMax=16 .
.PP
To accept LPD traffic from a trusted LAN subnet, override
.B ListenStream=
via
.B "systemctl edit cups\-lpd.socket"
and restrict source IP addresses with host firewall rules.
.SH SECURITY
RFC 1179 LPD provides no transport encryption and no strong client
authentication.
Do not expose TCP port 515 to untrusted networks.
Queue names are strictly validated to ASCII alphanumerics plus
.BR _ ,
.BR \- ,
.BR . ,
and
.B +
(max 127 bytes, rejecting leading hyphens and path traversal).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/cups/daemon/cups\-lpd
LPD bridge executable.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/cups\-lpd.socket
Systemd socket unit (loopback-only default).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/cups\-lpd@.service
Hardened per-connection service unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cupsd (8),
.BR cupsd.conf (5),
.BR lpr (1),
.BR lpq (1),
.BR lprm (1),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
